        "original_id": "e22b460c-1da4-5d70-b9d9-f46453269b84",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Latham, Boght Corners, Colonie, Albany County, Troy, New York\n- Roads: New York State Route 9R, New York State Route 470, U.S. Route 9, U.S. Route 4\n\nFacts:\n- New York State Route 9R is a north–south state highway in northeastern Albany County, New York.\n- New York State Route 9R leaves U.S. Route 9 in the hamlet of Latham and rejoins U.S. Route 9 in the hamlet of Boght Corners, and both hamlets are in the town of Colonie.\n- Boght Corners, also called Boght, is a hamlet in the town of Colonie in northern Albany County, New York, and it straddles U.S. Route 9.\n- New York State Route 470 extends 2.91 miles from an intersection with New York State Route 9R in the town of Colonie to a junction with U.S. Route 4 in the city of Troy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
